{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S5SO3FiberAction","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDTIndex"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEuler_eq_deltaLambda_via_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEuler_eq_deltaLambda_via_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN.lean#L220-L228","doc":"**The merged `n = 5` anchor `dtEuler = Δ_λ`, re-derived from the general\ncollapse** (not `decide`).  Same statement as\n`DeltaLambdaDTIndex.PartitionOf5.dtEuler_eq_deltaLambda`, obtained here as a\ncorollary of the all-`n` `dtEulerG_collapse` + the chirality parity — evidence\nthat the general identity subsumes the anchor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.dtEuler_eq_dtEulerG","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.dtEuler_eq_dtEulerG","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN.lean#L215-L218","doc":"The merged anchor's `PartitionOf5.dtEuler` is the general `dtEulerG` at\n`(nStat, dim)` — definitional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.parity_eq_w0_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.parity_eq_w0_sign","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN.lean#L196-L204","doc":"**(†) holds at the `n = 5` anchor** (via the corpus identity), so the\ngeometric leg is fully closed there: the a-function-parity chirality equals\nthe conjugate Young-subgroup longest-element sign for every `λ ⊢ 5`.  This is\nthe general lemma above discharged at the anchor — a witness that the\nconditional reduction is non-vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.parity_eq_w0_sign_of_nStat_eq_sumChoose2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.parity_eq_w0_sign_of_nStat_eq_sumChoose2","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN.lean#L185-L194","doc":"**Geometric-chirality leg, conditional on (†).**  If the a-function statistic\nequals the conjugate-partition binomial sum (`nStatList parts = sumChoose2\nconj`, i.e. (†) above), then the a-function-parity chirality equals the\ngeometric longest-element-sign formula `(-1)^{Σ_i C(λ'_i,2)}` for that\npartition.  The hypothesis `(†)` is the single remaining general-`n` gap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.dtEulerG_eq_deltaLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.dtEulerG_eq_deltaLambda","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN.lean#L161-L168","doc":"**Anchor subsumption**: the general DT Euler characteristic, evaluated at the\ncorpus `n = 5` data `(nStatList p.parts, p.dim)`, equals the corpus binding\nfactor `p.deltaLambda`.  Uses the *general* collapse plus the corpus chirality\nparity `deltaSign_eq_nStat_parity`; no per-partition `decide`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.nStat_eq_nStatList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.nStat_eq_nStatList","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN.lean#L157-L159","doc":"`PartitionOf5.nStat` is the general `nStatList` on the block's parts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.nStatList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.nStatList","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN.lean#L152-L155","doc":"The general a-function statistic on a partition's parts — the identical fold\nthat defines `PartitionOf5.nStat`, read on a general `List ℕ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEulerG_neg_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEulerG_neg_iff","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN.lean#L130-L143","doc":"**Sign leg, general `n`**: the DT Euler characteristic is negative iff the\na-function grade is odd and the dimension is positive (Behrend `(-1)^{dim}`\nis negative exactly on odd-dimensional moduli). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEulerG_magnitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEulerG_magnitude","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN.lean#L123-L128","doc":"**Magnitude leg, general `n`**: `(DT Euler)² = d²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEulerG_eq_deltaLambdaG","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEulerG_eq_deltaLambdaG","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN.lean#L115-L121","doc":"**THE GENERAL-`n` UNIFICATION.**  For EVERY partition (any a-function grade\n`N = n(λ)`, any Wedderburn dimension `d = dim V_λ`), the DT / 3d-index Euler\ncharacteristic equals the binding factor `Δ_λ`.  The horn-1 sign\n(`deltaSignParity N = (-1)^{n(λ)}`) and the horn-2 magnitude (`d = dim V_λ`)\nare the parity and value of ONE graded datum — for all `n`, not just `n = 5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.deltaLambdaG","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.deltaLambdaG","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN.lean#L112-L113","doc":"General per-partition binding factor `Δ_λ = deltaSign · dim`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.deltaSignParity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.deltaSignParity","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN.lean#L108-L110","doc":"General chirality sign = a-function parity `(-1)^{n(λ)}` (the corpus\n`deltaSign` at `n ≤ 5`, lifted to all `n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEulerG_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEulerG_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN.lean#L81-L99","doc":"**The general-`n` DT collapse (the real content, all `N, d`).**  The\nalternating Euler characteristic of a single-degree object collapses to the\nBehrend sign `(-1)^N` times the count `d`.  This is the `n`-free lift of the\nseven `decide`d instances in `DeltaLambdaDTIndex.lean`: proved once, by a\n`List.range` induction, for every grade `N` and dimension `d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEulerG","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEulerG","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN.lean#L76-L79","doc":"The DT / 3d-index graded Euler characteristic\n`χ = Σ_{k=0}^{N} (-1)^k · dim (G)_k` — a genuine finite alternating sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.gradedDimG","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.gradedDimG","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndexGeneralN.lean#L73-L74","doc":"Graded dimension of the single-degree object: `d` in degree `N`, else `0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}